<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><meta name="robots" content="noindex,nofollow"><title>Chinese 3 · Paper C · Learner paper</title><base href="/api/v1/course-tests/chinese-3/c/file/"><link rel="stylesheet" href="paper.css"></head><body><main><header class="hero"><p class="eyebrow">HSKKit · Chinese 3 Course Review · Original Paper C</p><h1>Learner paper</h1><p>40 objective questions + 4 writing/speaking tasks · 90-minute section budget.</p><p class="note">Reference materials. Open the workspace for section clocks, local answer saving and recording. Writing and speaking need self-review or your own teacher; no automatic grade.</p><nav class="links"><a href="index.html">Overview</a><a href="student.html">Learner paper</a><a href="student-traditional.html">繁體試卷</a><a href="teacher.html">Answers &amp; scripts</a><a href="listening.html">Listen to Chinese 3 C</a><a href="student.pdf">Learner PDF</a><a href="student-traditional.pdf">繁體 PDF</a><a href="teacher.pdf">Answer PDF</a></nav></header><nav class="links"><a href="#listening">Listening</a><a href="#reading">Reading</a><a href="#writing">Writing</a><a href="#speaking">Speaking</a></nav><h2 class="section-title" id="listening">Listening · 25 minutes</h2><h3>L1 · Questions 1–5</h3><audio controls preload="none" src="assets/audio/listening-group-1.mp3"></audio><p class="note">6:15 group track: 1 + 2 + 2 questions across three sources; each source plays twice, with answering pauses.</p><section class="material-block" data-material="C3C-L1a"><p class="eyebrow">Questions 1</p><p class="gloss">图书角: classroom book corner</p><div class="single-question"><article class="question" id="q1"><h3>1. When did the speaker first join an activity in the new class?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 去年九月开学前的最后一周</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 去年九月开学后的第二周</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 今年九月开学后的第一天</div></div></article></div></section><section class="material-block" data-material="C3C-L1b"><p class="eyebrow">Questions 2, 3 · Shared material</p><p class="gloss">软件: software</p><p class="gloss">资格: qualification</p><p class="gloss">标志: sign</p><div class="paired-questions"><article class="question" id="q2"><h3>2. What had the man originally thought he needed before helping?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 先把所有同学的住址记住</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 先请别人替他画上学路线</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 先学会很难的软件</div></div></article><article class="question" id="q3"><h3>3. Why does he prepare a route drawing for the next discussion?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 同学已经决定以后不再使用地图软件</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 他发现下午的小门已经改成全天开放</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 同学需要他熟悉的路线信息，不只是软件操作</div></div></article></div></section><section class="material-block" data-material="C3C-L1c"><p class="eyebrow">Questions 4, 5 · Shared material</p><p class="gloss">讲解: explanation</p><p class="gloss">对应: corresponding</p><div class="paired-questions"><article class="question" id="q4"><h3>4. What does the woman explicitly want to do first?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 马上完整看完讲解视频再读文章</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 独立读几分钟，找出自己不懂的地方</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 先把所有问题交给同伴代写</div></div></article><article class="question" id="q5"><h3>5. What best explains the man’s final arrangement?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 让视频代替原文，以后不必再读句子</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 要求所有人先提出完全相同的问题</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 保留独立阅读，也让视频回应实际遇到的问题</div></div></article></div></section><h3>L2 · Questions 6–10</h3><audio controls preload="none" src="assets/audio/listening-group-2.mp3"></audio><p class="note">6:15 group track: 1 + 2 + 2 questions across three sources; each source plays twice, with answering pauses.</p><section class="material-block" data-material="C3C-L2a"><p class="eyebrow">Questions 6</p><p class="gloss">短片: short video</p><p class="gloss">参观: visit/tour</p><div class="single-question"><article class="question" id="q6"><h3>6. What will the speaker do first for the holiday project?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 选三个地方写介绍，并排出参观顺序</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 先买新相机，再决定介绍哪些地方</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 把拍摄全部完成以后才准备介绍词</div></div></article></div></section><section class="material-block" data-material="C3C-L2b"><p class="eyebrow">Questions 7, 8 · Shared material</p><p class="gloss">耳机: headphones</p><p class="gloss">名额: available place</p><div class="paired-questions"><article class="question" id="q7"><h3>7. What does Course A require?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 有电脑和耳机，并连续四周按时参加</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 只带纸笔，任选一个周六参加</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 只在第一周借到电脑就能完成全部课程</div></div></article><article class="question" id="q8"><h3>8. Which next step fits the man’s circumstances?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 因为本周六没空，就放弃所有以后场次</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 询问乙下周的内容和名额，确认后单次报名</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 只借一周电脑，直接承诺上完甲四周</div></div></article></div></section><section class="material-block" data-material="C3C-L2c"><p class="eyebrow">Questions 9, 10 · Shared material</p><p class="gloss">片段: short extract</p><p class="gloss">顺序: sequence</p><div class="paired-questions"><article class="question" id="q9"><h3>9. Who is responsible for preparing the listening extract?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 小许</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 负责记录问题的女生</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 负责发出安排的男生</div></div></article><article class="question" id="q10"><h3>10. What sequence have they agreed on?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 一边播放一边讨论，直到讲完每道题</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 先独立听，再对答案，集中讨论两个问题</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 先等老师答复所有问题，再开始听音频</div></div></article></div></section><h3>L3 · Questions 11–15</h3><audio controls preload="none" src="assets/audio/listening-group-3.mp3"></audio><p class="note">6:15 group track: 1 + 2 + 2 questions across three sources; each source plays twice, with answering pauses.</p><section class="material-block" data-material="C3C-L3a"><p class="eyebrow">Questions 11</p><p class="gloss">校园广播: school radio broadcast</p><div class="single-question"><article class="question" id="q11"><h3>11. What is the main purpose of this broadcast?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 分享新同学选择学习地点的经历和理由</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 宣布全校每个学生必须使用的固定座位</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 只按座位数量给所有教室排名</div></div></article></div></section><section class="material-block" data-material="C3C-L3b"><p class="eyebrow">Questions 12, 13 · Shared material</p><p class="gloss">播音员: radio announcer</p><p class="gloss">停顿: pause</p><p class="gloss">交稿: submit a script/recording</p><div class="paired-questions"><article class="question" id="q12"><h3>12. How does Jilan’s approach change?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 从急着模仿声音，变为用自己的声音清楚表达内容</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 从自己写稿，变为请朋友代录全部节目</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 从检查内容，变为只追求说话速度</div></div></article><article class="question" id="q13"><h3>13. Which attitude is best supported by the ending?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 可以保留个人表达方式，同时认真检查是否说清楚</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 只要用自己的声音，就完全不必修改</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 只有听起来和播音员完全一样才值得发表</div></div></article></div></section><section class="material-block" data-material="C3C-L3c"><p class="eyebrow">Questions 14, 15 · Shared material</p><p class="gloss">提示牌: information sign</p><p class="gloss">小苗: young seedlings</p><p class="gloss">可重复使用: reusable</p><div class="paired-questions"><article class="question" id="q14"><h3>14. Which rule must participants follow during the check?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 为了看清提示牌，可以穿过所有草地</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 每个人必须自带满电手机和相机</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 走小路，不进入新种小苗的区域</div></div></article><article class="question" id="q15"><h3>15. Which plan lets the man contribute with his available resources?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 放弃记录，只能等买新手机后再参加</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 穿过小苗尽快拍照，以免手机电量用完</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 沿小路用记录板记问题，照片需要时请老师拍</div></div></article></div></section><h3>L4 · Questions 16–20</h3><audio controls preload="none" src="assets/audio/listening-group-4.mp3"></audio><p class="note">6:15 group track: 1 + 2 + 2 questions across three sources; each source plays twice, with answering pauses.</p><section class="material-block" data-material="C3C-L4a"><p class="eyebrow">Questions 16</p><p class="gloss">餐具: cutlery</p><p class="gloss">归还: return a borrowed item</p><div class="single-question"><article class="question" id="q16"><h3>16. When can students now collect the cutlery?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 周三午休</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 周四上课前</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 周四放学后</div></div></article></div></section><section class="material-block" data-material="C3C-L4b"><p class="eyebrow">Questions 17, 18 · Shared material</p><p class="gloss">戏剧社: drama club</p><p class="gloss">收获: something learned/gained</p><div class="paired-questions"><article class="question" id="q17"><h3>17. What does Xiaoxia now do before leaving detailed discussion until the weekend?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 每天晚上把所有群消息都重新读完</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 用十分钟记一个收获和一个问题</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 先退出戏剧社，不再和同伴交流</div></div></article><article class="question" id="q18"><h3>18. Which combination explains why she wants to continue this arrangement?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 她从此不看任何通知，也不准备上学用品</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 两周记录已经证明每个人都必须照此生活</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 先记下问题，周末再聊，减少每晚等消息且仍保留交流</div></div></article></div></section><section class="material-block" data-material="C3C-L4c"><p class="eyebrow">Questions 19, 20 · Shared material</p><p class="gloss">重点: main point</p><p class="gloss">塞进去: cram into</p><div class="paired-questions"><article class="question" id="q19"><h3>19. Which adjustment fits the woman’s short practice periods?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 每天增加到一小时，把所有细节都背下来</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 选一个重点，分次练开头和一个例子</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 等能一次讲完全部内容才开始任何练习</div></div></article><article class="question" id="q20"><h3>20. What changed view is supported by the man’s memory?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 介绍不必一次说完所有事，有意义的追问也值得重视</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 只要有人提问，准备内容就没有必要</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 任何超时的介绍都会得到完全一样的好结果</div></div></article></div></section><h2 class="section-title" id="reading">Reading · 30 minutes</h2><h3>R1 · Questions 21–25</h3><section class="material-block" data-material="C3C-R1a"><p class="eyebrow">Questions 21</p><div class="source"><p class="cn">去年三月，我转到现在的班级。第二次班会时，老师让大家给新同学写一张小卡片，介绍一个自己喜欢的校园地点。我收到的第一张上写着“午休来窗边的长桌，可以一起画画”。那天我没有马上去，只先回了一句谢谢。周五我带着纸笔去试了试，后来常在那里见到写卡片的人。</p></div><p class="gloss">转到: transfer to</p><p class="gloss">班会: class meeting</p><div class="single-question"><article class="question" id="q21"><h3>21. When did classmates write the cards for new students?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 去年三月转班前的最后一次活动</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 去年三月转班后的第二次班会</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 今年三月第一次参加绘画比赛时</div></div></article></div></section><section class="material-block" data-material="C3C-R1b"><p class="eyebrow">Questions 22, 23 · Shared material</p><div class="source"><p class="cn">刚转班时，小齐被邀请参加午休的桌面游戏。她以前只在家和弟弟玩，担心规则不一样，自己输了以后大家就不想再邀请她。第一轮她一直不敢问，走错了一步。她想收好东西离开，旁边的小文却把说明书转过来，请大家一起看那一条规则。<br>看完以后，小齐发现另外两个同学也记错了。他们重新试了一轮，还请她说说在家玩的不同方法。第二天她没有提前练到每一步都不会错，而是带了一张自己写的问题纸。有人建议换一种游戏时，她先问需要几个人、能玩多久，再决定参加。她后来记住的，不是第一轮输了多少，而是大家愿意把规则说明白的样子。</p></div><p class="gloss">桌面游戏: tabletop game</p><p class="gloss">规则: rules</p><p class="gloss">说明书: instruction booklet</p><div class="paired-questions"><article class="question" id="q22"><h3>22. What had Xiaoqi feared before the first round?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 其他同学会要求她先教弟弟玩</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 所有人都会拒绝查看说明书</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 输了以后大家不再邀请她</div></div></article><article class="question" id="q23"><h3>23. Why does she return with questions rather than trying to eliminate every possible mistake?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 因为她已经确定所有游戏规则都完全相同</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 共同查规则的经历表明，不懂时可以一起问清楚</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 因为小文替她承诺以后每次都一定赢</div></div></article></div></section><section class="material-block" data-material="C3C-R1c"><p class="eyebrow">Questions 24, 25 · Shared material</p><div class="source"><p class="cn">小组通知：周四下午六点前，每人交一份中文使用说明，只要文字，不用交视频。小岑负责把大家的内容放在同一页上，周五午休请新成员试读，看看步骤是否清楚。——小许<br>小川回复：学校借我的电脑今晚要归还，到周五才能再用。我已在纸上写好四个步骤，周四午休能借同伴的手机拍给你。每步的序号都在，第二步我加了一个例子。我想请你先看看照片里的字是否清楚；如果有地方太小，我午休还能重新拍。我担心你以为必须有视频，才一直想等电脑借回来。现在知道通知只要文字，就能按时准备了。</p></div><p class="gloss">序号: step number</p><p class="gloss">试读: try reading</p><div class="paired-questions"><article class="question" id="q24"><h3>24. What does each member have to submit by Thursday at 6 p.m.?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 一份中文文字使用说明，不必有视频</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 已经录好的完整中文演示视频</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 新成员周五试读后的全部反馈</div></div></article><article class="question" id="q25"><h3>25. How can Xiaocen keep Xiaochuan’s part on schedule for the Friday trial?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 等他周五借回电脑、补完视频后才开始整理</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 周四检查照片是否清楚，再整理其中的文字</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 只收电子打印稿，因此直接删掉他的部分</div></div></article></div></section><h3>R2 · Questions 26–30</h3><section class="material-block" data-material="C3C-R2a"><p class="eyebrow">Questions 26</p><div class="source"><p class="cn">暑假我想学设计活动海报。这周先找几份校园公告，比较标题、时间和地点放在哪里，再用纸笔给熟悉的社团画一张草稿。周末请同学只看草稿，找出报名时间。如果不好找，就先调整位置，不急着学复杂的软件。我希望开始学工具以前，先知道自己要让读者看清什么。</p></div><p class="gloss">海报: poster</p><p class="gloss">标题: heading/title</p><div class="single-question"><article class="question" id="q26"><h3>26. What is the writer’s immediate preparation for poster design?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 比较公告的信息位置，画草稿并请同学试读</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 先学会复杂软件，再第一次查看校园公告</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 印好所有正式海报后，才确认报名时间</div></div></article></div></section><section class="material-block" data-material="C3C-R2b"><p class="eyebrow">Questions 27, 28 · Shared material</p><div class="source"><p class="cn">假期项目公告：甲是故事剪辑，周二和周四上午各上一次课，报名时须已有一份故事脚本；费用四十元。乙是图文导览，周五下午上一次课，须带三张自己拍的地点照片和纸笔；免费。两项都可借用现场电脑，报名截止时间同为下周一中午。<br>小舟给同伴的回复：我下周二、周四上午要陪家人办事，周五下午有空。我最想把校园里容易走错的地方介绍清楚，上周已经拍了几张路口照片，还没有写故事脚本。我准备这个周末选出三张，想好每张要说明什么，周一登记前再确认乙是否有位置。电脑可以现场借，不必因为我家没有电脑就放弃。</p></div><p class="gloss">脚本: script</p><p class="gloss">图文导览: picture-and-text guide</p><div class="paired-questions"><article class="question" id="q27"><h3>27. Which difference between the projects is correctly stated?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 甲提供现场电脑，乙完全不许借电脑</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 甲要已有故事脚本，乙要自摄地点照片</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 甲免费，乙必须交四十元材料费</div></div></article><article class="question" id="q28"><h3>28. Which next step fits Xiaozhou’s interest, resources and schedule?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 先为甲写脚本，忽略周二和周四的时间冲突</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 选三张路口照片并确认乙名额，周一截止前登记</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 必须先买一台电脑，才有资格问乙的名额</div></div></article></div></section><section class="material-block" data-material="C3C-R2c"><p class="eyebrow">Questions 29, 30 · Shared material</p><div class="source"><p class="cn">校园广播通知：每组周五上午十点前交一段不超过一分钟的介绍录音，并附上完全对应的文字稿。不要只交背景音乐。小组可自己分工，不要求每个人都录音。老师会按文字稿核对听不清的地方。<br>小岚：我想写文字稿，坐车时也能在本子上改。小陆：我家晚上比较安静，我来录音，不过希望先有确定的内容，不想一边录一边等修改。小岚：周三我先发草稿，大家周四午休核对，晚上你录。周五九点我们一起听一次，九点半把录音和最后文字稿一起交。小陆：好，临时改了词也要在文字稿上改，不能留下两个不同版本。</p></div><p class="gloss">对应: correspond exactly</p><p class="gloss">版本: version</p><div class="paired-questions"><article class="question" id="q29"><h3>29. Why does Xiaolan offer to write the script?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 坐车时也可以在本子上修改</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 她家晚上比所有人家里都安静</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 通知规定每个人必须各录一段</div></div></article><article class="question" id="q30"><h3>30. Which plan meets both the notice and the group’s agreement?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 周五九点半只交音乐，文字稿下周再补</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 周四录好旧稿，周五改文字但不检查是否对应</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 周四核稿后录音，周五九点半交对应的两份材料</div></div></article></div></section><h3>R3 · Questions 31–35</h3><section class="material-block" data-material="C3C-R3a"><p class="eyebrow">Questions 31</p><div class="source"><p class="cn">校园节目本周介绍原创短故事《路过的窗》。主人公每天急着走同一条路，后来为新同学带路，才第一次停下来看窗边的介绍牌。节目不把他变成无所不知的向导，而是选取前后两次经过同一地点的片段，请听众比较他注意了什么。想讨论日常细节的同学，可以带一个问题来听。</p></div><p class="gloss">向导: guide</p><p class="gloss">无所不知: know everything</p><div class="single-question"><article class="question" id="q31"><h3>31. What does the programme invite listeners to compare?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 人物前后经过同一地点时注意到的内容</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 所有校园向导背诵地名的速度</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 两所不同学校里窗户的数量</div></div></article></div></section><section class="material-block" data-material="C3C-R3b"><p class="eyebrow">Questions 32, 33 · Shared material</p><div class="source"><p class="cn">原创故事《没送到的卡片》里，新来的安禾看到同学们周末活动的照片，却没有收到邀请。她以为大家不想带她一起，第二天把原来准备的小礼物收进了抽屉。午休时，小林来问她为什么没到，还拿出一张写着旧教室号码的邀请卡，才知道他一直把卡放在她以前班级的桌上。<br>安禾先说自己昨天有些难过，又问下一次活动怎样确认时间地点。她没有假装什么也没发生，也没有继续不问就认定别人不欢迎她。后来小林把新卡递到她手里，她读了一遍时间，再请他指给自己看集合处。礼物仍在抽屉里，她想等下次真正见面时再带过去。</p></div><p class="gloss">邀请卡: invitation card</p><p class="gloss">抽屉: drawer</p><p class="gloss">集合处: meeting point</p><div class="paired-questions"><article class="question" id="q32"><h3>32. How does Anhe’s understanding change after the conversation?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 从不想参加，变为被要求立刻送出礼物</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 从已经收到卡片，变为认定照片中的活动是假的</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 从认为被排斥，变为知道邀请卡放错了班级</div></div></article><article class="question" id="q33"><h3>33. Which conclusion is best supported by her final actions?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 她愿意表达感受，也通过核对具体信息继续参与</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 她认定每次没收到邀请都一定只是教室号码错了</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 她决定以后只要有照片就不必问时间地点</div></div></article></div></section><section class="material-block" data-material="C3C-R3c"><p class="eyebrow">Questions 34, 35 · Shared material</p><div class="source"><p class="cn">绿地提示牌提案：用美术室剩下的硬纸板做牌，写清可以走的小路和不能进入的新种苗区。学校提供可重复使用的夹子和支架，牌子夹在支架上，不往树上钉，也不为每个经过的人另印一张。每组先画草稿，请老师看清楚后再写正式牌。<br>补充通知：周六上午有雨，大家十点先到美术室做牌，不到绿地放置。等天晴且老师在场时，再一起讨论放在哪里。小余只有周六上午能来，希望自己的部分那天做完。她可以先负责画清楚一块牌的路线，核对后把成品牌留在美术室，另请以后有空的组员随老师放置，而不是自己下雨时抢先把牌钉到树上。</p></div><p class="gloss">硬纸板: cardboard</p><p class="gloss">支架: stand</p><p class="gloss">放置: put in position</p><div class="paired-questions"><article class="question" id="q34"><h3>34. What does the school provide for displaying the signs?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 每位路人一份新印的纸本</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 可重复使用的夹子和支架</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 把牌钉到树上所需的工具</div></div></article><article class="question" id="q35"><h3>35. Which plan fits Xiaoyu’s availability and both notices?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 为周六做完全部步骤，下雨时自己把牌钉到树上</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 周六室内核稿做牌，留给有空组员随老师择晴天放置</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 直接跳过草稿和核对，让路人各领一张新纸</div></div></article></div></section><h3>R4 · Questions 36–40</h3><section class="material-block" data-material="C3C-R4a"><p class="eyebrow">Questions 36</p><div class="source"><p class="cn">本周绿地观察活动试行少印纸：路线说明放在集合处的大字公共板上，不给每个人自动发一份。需要近处阅读，或要带回家核对时间的同学，仍可领取纸本。这个办法只先用于本次活动，不等于以后所有通知都改成电子版。结束后，负责人会收集大家的使用意见，再决定下一次怎样做。</p></div><p class="gloss">试行: trial implementation</p><p class="gloss">纸本: paper copy</p><div class="single-question"><article class="question" id="q36"><h3>36. Which description matches the reduced-printing trial?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 本次用公共板为主，有需要的人仍可领纸本</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 从此所有通知只能在网上看，完全不发纸本</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 无论参加者是否需要，每人自动发三份路线表</div></div></article></div></section><section class="material-block" data-material="C3C-R4b"><p class="eyebrow">Questions 37, 38 · Shared material</p><div class="source"><p class="cn">小安的记录：刚参加摄影社时，我每个周六跟着大家连跑几个地方，想多拍一些照片，回家后却没时间整理，也觉得很赶。最近两周，我改成上午只在一个地方观察四十五分钟，拍完先选几张、写下注意到什么。这两个周六的下午，我都没有再赶去下一个地点，而是留在家里休息或做别的事。<br>同伴回复：你还想观察有意思的细节，也想让周末有空余，可以再试几次这个安排。照片少了，不等于没有学习。小安补充：我想下周看看遇到社团特别活动时怎样调整。现在只记录了两个周六，不能说所有人少去几个地方都会有一样的感受，也不能认定以后永远不换地点。</p></div><p class="gloss">摄影社: photography club</p><p class="gloss">空余: free time</p><div class="paired-questions"><article class="question" id="q37"><h3>37. What change does Xiaoan explicitly report over the two Saturdays?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 已经决定以后永远不再更换拍摄地点</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 上午不再拍照，也不整理任何照片</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 下午没有再赶去下一个拍摄地点</div></div></article><article class="question" id="q38"><h3>38. Why does the reply suggest trying this arrangement a few more times?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 因为两周已证明只拍四十五分钟适合所有人</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 因为照片一少，摄影社就不再要求任何学习</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 它保留观察细节的兴趣，也回应周末想有空余的需要</div></div></article></div></section><section class="material-block" data-material="C3C-R4c"><p class="eyebrow">Questions 39, 40 · Shared material</p><div class="source"><p class="cn">刚到新班时，我参加了一次校园介绍活动，提前把许多地名背了下来，怕别人问什么我都不会。真正开始以后，我很少用到那些长说明。带队的同学反而请我说一个自己想了解的问题，大家一起去找答案。我问了图书角什么时候能借书，后来另一位新同学说，她也一直想问。<br>现在我准备参加新的社团介绍，每周只有两次午休能做准备。我决定先写两个真实的问题，再看相关通知，不把每个角落的名称都背一遍。遇到还不能确定的内容，就标出来当场询问。上次我以为准备得越多、说得越长越好，这次出门前检查的是：问题是否清楚，哪些已有答案，哪些还要一起找。</p></div><p class="gloss">带队: lead a group</p><p class="gloss">当场: on the spot</p><div class="paired-questions"><article class="question" id="q39"><h3>39. Which preparation fits both the earlier experience and the present time limit?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 继续背所有长说明，直到每个地名都完全记熟</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 不准备任何问题，认定别人一定会替自己问完</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 先准备两个真实问题，查相关通知并标出待询问处</div></div></article><article class="question" id="q40"><h3>40. What changed view is supported by the final checklist?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 准备可以更有针对性，保留尚需一起找答案的问题</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 只要问题真实，就完全不必查任何现有通知</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 在新班级里，只有背出最多地名的人才算参与</div></div></article></div></section><h2 class="section-title" id="writing">Writing · 25 minutes</h2><p>W1 and W2 share 25 minutes. Use paper or your own editor; this review page does not save answers.</p><section class="box" id="W1"><p class="eyebrow">writing · W1</p><h2>Reply to an earlier media-project deadline</h2><p>Reply to Zhou in Chinese. Say whether you can join Tuesday’s lunchtime topic meeting. Choose a campus-corner introduction, a new-student question-and-answer programme or another relevant topic and explain why. State a part you can prepare. Give a feasible plan for the earlier Thursday deadline, and ask one relevant clarification or confirmation. About 60-90 Chinese characters is guidance, not a minimum.</p><div class="source"><p class="cn">小安：我们要做校园广播项目，你周二午休能来选题吗？你更想介绍校园角落，还是做新同学问答？你能准备哪部分？原来周五晚上交，现在改为周四下午六点前，录音和文字稿都要一起交。请提个能按时完成的办法，也问清你还需要知道的事。<br>小舟</p></div><ul class="checklist"><li>Answer whether you can attend Tuesday lunchtime.</li><li>Choose a relevant topic and explain a reason.</li><li>State a part you can prepare.</li><li>Propose preparation and submission that fit the earlier Thursday deadline.</li><li>Ask one relevant clarification or confirmation.</li></ul><p class="badge">Manual /8 · no automatic grade</p></section><section class="box" id="W2"><p class="eyebrow">writing · W2</p><h2>A learning experience that changed an expectation</h2><p>Use the fictional activity card to write connected Chinese paragraphs about a learning experience that changed your view. Include time and context, at least two actions in sequence, expectation versus outcome, a reason or feeling, and one reflection or next step. Add plausible details consistent with the card if useful. About 140-180 Chinese characters is guidance, not a minimum.</p><div class="source"><p class="cn">虚构学习卡<br>时间：上个月一个周日下午<br>地点与活动：活动中心，第一次学折纸<br>原先期待：看图很简单，几分钟完成，还想带一个给朋友<br>经过：只看最后的样子，两次没做好；展开纸；与同伴逐步看图，发现第二步方向反了；重做<br>结果：花时比预计长，但做出能立起来的纸房子，也能说明改了哪里<br>感受与下一步：自行选择，须与事实一致</p></div><ul class="checklist"><li>Establish last month’s Sunday afternoon and a first paper-folding session.</li><li>Describe one action from the card.</li><li>Describe a second action in a consistent sequence.</li><li>Contrast the original expectation with the actual outcome.</li><li>Explain a feeling or a reason.</li><li>Give a specific reflection or next step.</li></ul><p class="badge">Manual /8 · no automatic grade</p></section><h2 class="section-title" id="speaking">Speaking · 10 minutes</h2><section class="box" id="S1"><p class="eyebrow">speaking · S1</p><h2>Choose and adapt learning-support materials</h2><p>Respond in Chinese to four fixed prompts from a classmate planning a Chinese-learning support activity. Each file already includes two plays; play the file once, then prepare for 15 seconds and respond for up to 30 seconds. Explain a preference using an experience, adapt to a new resource limit and agree on a next step. Personal details may be invented. All four turns together form one task /8, not an adaptive conversation.</p><p>You and a classmate will run a short Chinese-learning support activity. A change of resources is introduced in the third prompt.</p><ul class="checklist"><li>State a preference or learning need with a reason.</li><li>Link a past experience to that preference.</li><li>Adapt materials to no internet while a computer remains available.</li><li>Give a final arrangement, own preparation and a relevant confirmation.</li></ul><h3>S1-1</h3><audio controls preload="none" src="assets/audio/s1-1.mp3"></audio><h3>S1-2</h3><audio controls preload="none" src="assets/audio/s1-2.mp3"></audio><h3>S1-3</h3><audio controls preload="none" src="assets/audio/s1-3.mp3"></audio><h3>S1-4</h3><audio controls preload="none" src="assets/audio/s1-4.mp3"></audio><p class="note">Each file already plays the prompt twice. Play it once; then prepare for 15 seconds and respond for up to 30 seconds. Four responses are one /8 task.</p><p class="badge">Manual /8 · no automatic grade</p></section><section class="box" id="S2"><p class="eyebrow">speaking · S2</p><h2>Compare two learning-support plans</h2><p>Recommend one of the two learning-support plans to your class. Compare a relevant feature of both, use two different details from the card to support your choice, acknowledge a limitation and propose a practical next step. Either plan can receive full credit if its constraints and actual participation are addressed. Prepare for 60 seconds and speak for up to 120 seconds. Use the on-screen card; there is no separate audio question.</p><div class="source"><p class="cn">班级情况：18人，周二、三、四午休都有空；其中13人周六上午有空。希望尽量让更多人获得支持，也重视提问机会；总材料预算50元。<br>甲：周二、三、四午休各一场，12:40–13:00，每场最多6人，每人本周只报一场；免费；周一17:00前按场次登记并交问题。三场各有6个位置，按确认名单参加。<br>乙：周六9:00–10:30集中学习，最多18人；全组材料费40元；周四18:00前报名，须带自己的问题卡。不能参加者可领取已有资料，但不算参加现场讨论。<br>可以推荐任一方案，须说明实际参与范围、时间、准备与限制。</p></div><ul class="checklist"><li>Compare a relevant feature of both plans.</li><li>Make a clear recommendation.</li><li>Use one supporting detail from the card.</li><li>Use a different supporting detail from the card.</li><li>Acknowledge a limitation of the recommended plan.</li><li>Give a feasible next step addressing the limitation.</li></ul><p class="badge">Manual /8 · no automatic grade</p></section></main></body></html>